    "summary": "This work describes a Knoevenagel condensation reaction using surface-immobilized ZnNx sites as Lewis acid catalysts. The reaction proceeds through Lewis acid activation followed by nucleophilic attack in aqueous solvent. Under flow conditions, the process achieved 99% yield with a 60-minute residence time at 0.1 mL/min flow rate using 0.2 M substrate concentration at room temperature. The flow setup utilized a back pressure regulator at 1.0 bar and operated in single-phase liquid regime. Flow chemistry enabled the reaction to proceed at room temperature while maintaining excellent yields, whereas the batch process required heating to 200°C, demonstrating significant energy savings and process intensification through improved heat and mass transfer in the continuous flow reactor.",
